{"availability":"available","full":"supermedium/aframe-react","name":"aframe-react","description":":atom: Build virtual reality experiences with A-Frame and React.","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":1429,"forks":149,"created":"2015-12-16T23:33:37Z","updated":"2024-06-19T15:56:27Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://ngokevin.github.io/aframe-react-boilerplate/","topics":["aframe","react","virtual-reality","vr","webvr"],"demo":"https://ngokevin.github.io/aframe-react-boilerplate/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T20:59:47.013Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T20:59:47.013Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T20:59:47.013Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T20:59:47.013Z","discoveredVia":[{"kind":"curated-list","name":"Awesome React Components","url":"https://github.com/brillout/awesome-react-components"}],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T20:59:47.013Z","stars":1429,"forks":149}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["I recommend using vanilla A-Frame and aframe-state-component with static templating over aframe-react. React wastes a lot of cycles and incurs a lot of memory garbage. aframe-react is often abused where it is too easy to place 3D/real-time logic at the React layer, causing poor performance (e.g., doing React renders on ticks). aframe-react applications frequently ignore the prescribed ECS framework of A-Frame. Internally, React does tons of computation to compute what changed, and flushes it to the entire application. It is apparent React ecosystem does not care much about memory as most…","A-Frame is a web framework for building virtual reality experiences. Since A-Frame is built on top of the DOM, web libraries such as React, Vue.js, Angular, Ember.js, d3.js are able to sit cleanly on top of A-Frame.","A-Frame is an entity-component-system (ECS) framework exposed through HTML. ECS is a pattern used in game development that favors composability over inheritance, which is more naturally suited to 3D scenes where objects are built of complex appearance, behavior, and functionality. In A-Frame, HTML attributes map to components which are composable modules that are plugged into s to attach appearance, behavior, and functionality."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/supermedium/aframe-react/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"4c5f7b4eb5184e55a43cde51289e8bf30b600a29094b46c58c002ef0f757cd9f","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T20:59:47.013Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T20:59:47.013Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"I recommend using vanilla A-Frame and aframe-state-component with static templating over aframe-react. React wastes a lot of cycles and incurs a lot of memory garbage. aframe-react is often abused where it is too easy to place 3D/real-time logic at the React layer, causing poor performance (e.g., doing React renders on ticks). aframe-react applications frequently ignore the prescribed ECS framework of A-Frame. Internally, React does tons of computation to compute what changed, and flushes it to the entire application. It is apparent React ecosystem does not care much about memory as most…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/supermedium/aframe-react/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"4c5f7b4eb5184e55a43cde51289e8bf30b600a29094b46c58c002ef0f757cd9f","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/supermedium/aframe-react/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T20:59:47.013Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2024-06-19T15:56:27Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/supermedium/aframe-react/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T20:59:47.013Z","hash":"4c5f7b4eb5184e55a43cde51289e8bf30b600a29094b46c58c002ef0f757cd9f","originalBytes":12519,"storedBytes":12519,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["react","a-frame","aframe-react","event","web","applications","data","component","objects","ecs","import","state","what","behavior",